  "verbalization": "Diospyrin appears to have a shared target relationship with SNU1 through a series of molecular pathways involving phosphodiesterase 6C. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Pronuciferine, Vitetrifolin B, and Norgestomet, all of which directly interact with SNU1. The evidence suggests that Diospyrin may modulate the activity of phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn influences the function of SNU1. The consistent presence of phosphodiesterase 6C as a common target across these compounds implies a potential mechanism by which Diospyrin could interact with SNU1, possibly through the regulation of intracellular signaling or metabolic processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of phosphodiesterase 6C in mediating the effects of these compounds on SNU1, offering a plausible mechanism for the observed relationship.",
